      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Endometrial ossification is a rare and benign pathology. The etiopathogenesis of this pathology is controversial. Findings suggestive of diagnosis are fairly well know, menstrual irregularities is the main clinical symptoms, expulsion of bony fragments is a rare but pathognomonic event. Pelvic ultrasonography suggested an intrauterine foreign body and hysteroscopy was necessary to make the correct diagnosis. Six cases of endometrial ossification diagnosis and treated at obstetrics and gynaecology department A of centre of La Rabta teaching hospital (Tunis) are reported."},
